PLATFORM PRODUCT MANUAL — Q1 2025
Document ID: PM-2025-Q1
Classification: Internal Use

FAQ: How do I configure webhook notifications?
Webhooks can be configured from the Developer Settings > Webhooks page. Click "Add Webhook", provide the target URL, select the events you want to subscribe to (minimum: deployment.completed, build.failed), and optionally set a secret token for payload signature verification. The platform sends a test ping to validate the endpoint. Webhook payloads are signed using HMAC-SHA256 with the provided secret.

FAQ: What is the maximum payload size for API requests?
The maximum request payload size is 10 MB for REST API calls. For file uploads via the Assets API, the limit is 250 MB per file. Requests exceeding these limits return HTTP 413 (Payload Too Large).

FAQ: How do I enable audit logging?
Audit logging is available on Enterprise plans. Navigate to Settings > Security > Audit Logs. Enable "Detailed Activity Logging" and select which event categories to capture: Authentication Events, API Access, Configuration Changes, and Data Export. Audit logs are retained for 90 days by default (configurable up to 365 days on request).
